{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967088-any-story-you-would-like-to-see-being-remade-remake-d","id":967088,"title":"Any story you would like to see being Remade/Remake'd ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-10T19:40:18-07:00","id":967088,"title":"Any story you would like to see being Remade/Remake'd ?","content":"honestly, i would love to see The Chaos Factor with a more &quot;Down to Earth&quot; Sam Height, or a &quot;Midnight Carnival&quot; considering the AMH: FreakShow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:18:05-07:00","id":967975,"title":"","content":"I'd say, <i>Chaos Factor </i>and <i>Montreal by Night</i>. Both had a &quot;demon problem&quot; where Demons/Infernalists could do pretty much anything.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind having Demons replaced with the Fallen from DtF (or something similar).<br /> It would also be great if they updated and downgraded the vampires in both books, and reduce the exaggerated number of Infernalists (where are the non-infernalists?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:43:18-07:00","id":968198,"title":"","content":"Personally, now that I have <i>Mexico City by Night</i> in my grubby little hands I'd prefer to not be reminded that <i>Chaos Factor</i> ever existed in the first place. <i>Montreal by Night</i> could certainly use a new edition that doesn't read as if it were written by the Warrens or Father Gabriele Amorth though, and one with an eye toward how vampires of various ages should be constructed stat-wise. I'd like to see the coven-centric approach of that book retained for any updates or other Sabbat citybooks\u2014I thought it was a nice departure from the way Camarilla cities are organized and gave a good feel for the Sabbat mindset. (When it's not being corrupted by the infernalists hiding under every bed, anyway....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T18:36:59-07:00","id":968291,"title":"","content":"Infernalists do not hide under the bed. They are living in luxury apartments while normal vampires are wading through the sewers. If you are going to be damned for eternity, you are sure as Hell going to make sure you are comfortable in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:52:54-07:00","id":968516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/967088-any-story-you-would-like-to-see-being-remade-remake-d?p=968291#post968291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernalists do not hide under the bed. They are living in luxury apartments while normal vampires are wading through the sewers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, In Revised. But here we're talking about the old editions.<br /> <br /> From what you said, you're obviously not familiar with the story. Because no, in the old editions, many of them lived in the sewers or similar poor conditions. Not many of them lived in luxury apartments (Galbraith was one of the few).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> What he meant (well, what I think he meant) by &quot;under every bed&quot; was that, in the old sabbat editions, you couldn't throw a rock without hitting an infernalist. Worse, they had plot-device powers (worse than Antideluvians).<br /> <br /> Infernalists and their Decani could do pretty much anything and pull any convenient trick out of their asses at any moment. Which made for very boring games and poor written stories.<br /> <br /> Now, Revised fixed it. They improved/balanced infernalist and Decani power. They shifted the focus away from Infernalism as the main theme.<br /> <br /> As a result <i>Mexico</i> has a better story than <i>Montreal</i>, but it would be great if <i>Montreal</i> was updated to Revised standards. (that means, no cartoonish Infernalists, no neonates with 30 discipline dots and no &quot;every sabbat is on a path with crazy magic&quot;). </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-13-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:49:19-07:00","id":972744,"title":"","content":"Exactly, Pleiades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:14:34-07:00","id":973917,"title":"","content":"Rage Across New York and Mage: Las Vegas.<br /> <br /> I really wish a good city book for werewolf with a sample-by the numbers sept. Same for las Vegas for mage. Something i can point out and said &quot;typical werewolf/ascension&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}